From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 15:21:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Name no higher layer in cat-harness text
 (check:reference-direction)

cat-harness#1116's full tier at aafb457 had one new failure,
cat-harness-tools:check:reference-direction:check: the new text named
layers above cat-harness. Reworded generically, keeping each rule:
- remote-mount: the cross-layer example says "a content layer" and "the
  tools layer"; the mutual-dependence example describes the case without
  the content layer's PR number; layer health says "the tools layer".
- merge-manager-watcher: the exception's example, and "What this does not
  do yet", name no tools PR numbers.
- prepare-merge: "two such checks in the tools layer".
The evidence stays in the earlier commit messages (folio-assistant-core
#654 and #639; cat-harness-tools #1514, #1564, #1603, #1610, #1616,
#1624 and #1625). check:reference-direction passes on the composed checkout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VQDpPc2tT1vUufdyDbQTBz
